{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/363507-poison-gifts","id":363507,"title":"Poison Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-08T08:12:26-08:00","id":363507,"title":"Poison Gifts","content":"Is there any Werewolf book that details a set of Gifts related to poison or the like? Alternatively, has anyone come up with a set of Poison (or Venom, etc) Gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T09:20:16-08:00","id":363589,"title":"","content":"Closest thing I could think of would be the Fever and Disease gifts, which aren't really poison but could be described as such.<br /> <br /> In <i>Night Horrors: Wolfsbane</i>, there's a Fire-touched who has the Rite of the Toxic Scar, which bonds their body with a spirit of poison, which serves as a familiar for a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T16:15:14-08:00","id":363902,"title":"","content":"Oh there's an idea! Check the pure book for fire touched gifts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T16:16:27-08:00","id":363903,"title":"","content":"Poison gifts could be cool to see if someone would be willing to write up a fan version. I'm inclined to think, personally that the gift list would be more focused on making mundane poisons and toxins more effective on werewolves rather than doing some kind of crazy shit with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T16:20:35-08:00","id":363907,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that enhancing mundane poisons would be more along the lines of Talens or Fetishes. I'm actually working on a Corruption gift for an upcoming chronicle. It features how poison or corruption is done through the lens of the different renown. I'll post it up after the 2nd edition drops and I have a full write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T16:32:43-08:00","id":363914,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of talens and fetishes involving poisons, at least a lot more than gifts.<br /> <br /> @The Scorpion I think the only problem with that is it just makes the gift too focused. It would literally be something that could only be used on werewolves, and so only useful to other werewolves who intended on being poisoners of their own kind, which is probably a small population.<br /> <br /> Another poison gift is Poisoned Essence, which causes 1 bashing damage for every point of essence the target uses. While this is useful on werewolves, it also has uses against spirits and claimed and ridden and so forth.<br /> <br /> In 2e, the Urshul form can cause tilts. I'm hoping that, if not naturally, there will be some ability for them to inflict the poisoned tilt on their enemies. It might require a lodge or a merit or some theft of power from the azlu or beshilu, but it seems like something that should be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-08-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:24:08-08:00","id":367448,"title":"","content":"A Gift of Poison/Venom is on my 'list of Gifts I want to do for 2e', though a poison Facet or two might just fit nicely into a Gift of Disease if we redo that for the 2e Pure at some point.<br /> <br /> Barring that, it should be fairly trivial to knock together a Rite or Fetish to do the job. Fetishes actually now include a category of function that I explicitly put in to allow for 'overwriting' new Facets into the game without having to write entire new Gifts with a full five Facets in them. The existing Gifts of Death or Nature would both seem solid candidates based on how the poison works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:12:16-08:00","id":367485,"title":"","content":"Fascinating. Thanks for the responses!<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, from what I know of 2e Gifts, I could see the facets maybe looking something like this:<br /> <br /> Cunning: Coat your claws/fangs in poison with a Toxicity = Cunning + Primal Urge.<br /> Glory: ???<br /> Honor: Cure/immunize someone of/against poison.<br /> Purity: Purge toxins from own body, gain a bonus on next attack roll against poisoner.<br /> Wisdom: Change one kind of poison into another; increase or reduce Toxicity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:33:55-08:00","id":367599,"title":"","content":"Honor and Purity kinda overlap, and Wisdom isn't self-sufficient. Cunning is too powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:42:35-08:00","id":367608,"title":"","content":"I need to read up on renown, I keep forgetting what purity is of.<br /> <br /> If you went that way Cunning might let you administer poison with a touch, rather than an attack that injects it. Maybe spit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:44:25-08:00","id":367610,"title":"","content":"Hmm fair enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T01:34:47-08:00","id":369605,"title":"","content":"My idea would be mixing it up a bit more with drugs, considering that the difference between a poison and a drug is that the drug isn't neccessarily lethal. But they both work with the theme of changing body-chemistry.<br /> <br /> Purity: Purging/enhancing resistance against poisons and drugs, both in self and others.<br /> Glory: Increase fighting ability while the werewolf in question is under the influence of drugs or poison.<br /> Honor: No idea, can't figure out a way to make something honourable with this.<br /> Wisdom: Locate and study poisons/drugs, and learn their effects,<br /> Cunning: Apply some debilitating poison that penalizes actions for a short while, but doesn't actually do damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T13:51:41-08:00","id":372859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/363507-poison-gifts?p=369605#post369605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honor: No idea, can't figure out a way to make something honourable with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>A subject is grazed with claws or nipped lightly. For the rest of the scene, every time they lie or they commit some sort of crime, they receive 1 point of Bashing Damage. Good for an Uratha courtroom with an Elodoth judge presiding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T04:38:29-08:00","id":374168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/363507-poison-gifts?p=372859#post372859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A subject is grazed with claws or nipped lightly. For the rest of the scene, every time they lie or they commit some sort of crime, they receive 1 point of Bashing Damage. Good for an Uratha courtroom with an Elodoth judge presiding.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah... that kinda makes sense. The ability to delay the effects of a poison or drug, based on the target's actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}